            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary><h3>Is protein hot chocolate good for weight loss?</h3></summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>
                  It can help as a low-calorie treat. The packets on this list are about 80 calories with 15 g of protein and 2 to 3 g of sugar, per their labels, compared with far more sugar in a café hot chocolate. Protein helps with fullness. Whether it helps you lose weight depends on your total intake, so count the milk and any toppings you add.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary><h3>Is chocolate protein powder high in lead?</h3></summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>
                  Chocolate powders tend to test higher for lead and cadmium than vanilla, because cocoa itself carries both metals. Results vary widely between products. Premier Protein's chocolate whey was reported at about 77% of Consumer Reports' cautious daily level of concern per serving in 2026. Keeping chocolate protein to one serving a day and choosing tested products is a sensible approach.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary><h3>Can I have protein hot chocolate after bariatric surgery?</h3></summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>
                  Many bariatric programs allow low-sugar protein drinks, and brands such as BariWise design hot chocolate specifically for that diet. However, when you can have warm drinks, milk and sweeteners depends on your stage and your surgical team's protocol. Ask your surgeon or registered dietitian before adding any product. This page is general information, not medical advice.
